----------------------------------------
Classdiagram for esp32 a host
classDiagram
direction LR

note for ESP32_A_Host "main function"
note for UART "Custom library "
note for USB "Official library (ESP-IDF provided)"
class ESP32_A_Host {
    MouseEvent
    KeyboardEvent
    DataFrame
  +setup()
  +loop()
  +Serial.begin()
}

class UART {
    BAUD, PIN_TX, PIN_RX
  +uart2_init()
  +sendFrame(dx,dy,btn)
}
class USB {
    event_queue: QueueHandle_t
  + install()
  + uninstall()
  + handleEvents()
  + deviceOpen()
  + deviceStart()
  + deviceClose()

}


    ESP32_A_Host --> UART : uart.h
    ESP32_A_Host --> USB  : usb_host.h

    style UART fill::#f66,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray: 5 5
    style USB fill::#f66,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray: 5 5
   

-----------------------------------------------------
flowchart!! Version for system test and quick demo
flowchart LR
    subgraph setup
    A[**Configration**] --> B[**UART0/2 init**]
    end
    subgraph loop
    B --> C[**Wait data from PC**]
    C --> D{bytes = 3?}
    D -- No --> C
    D -- Yes --> E[**CRC package**]
    E --> F[**sendFrame**]
    F --> G[**Report to PC**]
    G --> C
    end

------------------------------------------------------
flowchart!! Version for USB Host
flowchart LR
classDef inprogress fill:#f96,color:#fff
  subgraph setup & configuration
  A[**usb_host init**] --> B[**register tasks/callbacks**]
  end
  subgraph loop
  B --> C[**wait for device**]
  C --> D[**identify HID device**]
  D --> E[**handshake/start**]
  E:::inprogress --> F[**communicate reports/sendFrame**]
  F:::inprogress --device removed --> C
  end






